# src/syncai_driver_manager, from SyncAI-Robot-Driver-Manager: the UDP bridge to
# the gait controller. Managed with vcstool, the same way interface.repos manages
# src/syncai_common, robot-state.repos manages src/syncai_robot_state and
# third-party.repos manages src/third-party/.
#
#   vcs import < driver-manager.repos          # populate a fresh clone
#   vcs import < driver-manager.repos --force  # re-checkout after changing the pin
#
# The key already carries `src/`, so run this from the workspace root without an
# extra `src` argument, or the package lands in `src/src/`.
#
# It left this repository in 2026-10, when the rclcpp node was replaced by an
# rclrs (Rust) one that keeps the ROS surface unchanged (syncai_robot_state
# followed it out the same month): same package name, same
# `driver_manager_node` executable, same `driver_manager.launch.py`, so the two
# session specs in config/sessions/ did not move. What did change is inside the
# package: `params/driver_manager_params.yaml` is keyed on a bare `/**` instead of
# `/**/driver_manager`, because rclrs matches a params-file key only when it is
# exactly `/**` or exactly the node's fully-qualified name -- it does not expand
# `/**/<node>`, so the old key matched nothing and every parameter (the six
# velocity scales included) silently fell back to its code default.
#
# `src/syncai_driver_manager/` is gitignored -- edit the node in that checkout
# (its own git repo) and commit there, never here; the next --force import
# overwrites anything uncommitted.
#
# Tracks `dev`, that repo's default and working branch, like interface.repos:
# `main` lags behind it.
#
# HTTPS rather than the SSH remote: the repo is public, so the build container
# needs no keys. `git@github.com:chungweeeei/SyncAI-Robot-Driver-Manager.git` is
# the same checkout for anyone who prefers to push over SSH.
#
# BUILDING IT NEEDS THE IMAGE'S UNDERLAY TOO. It is an `ament_cargo` package: the
# robot image carries the Rust toolchain (rustup, cargo-ament-build, colcon-cargo
# / colcon-ros-cargo, libclang-dev -- see the Dockerfile's Rust stanza), which is
# NOT
# the Rust message crates on their own. rclrs's bindings for std_msgs / sensor_msgs /
# geometry_msgs / std_srvs / syncai_common are generated at build time by
# rosidl_generator_rs, which the image provides as a ros2-rust underlay at
# /opt/ros2_rust_underlay (the Dockerfile's underlay stanza) -- the same is true
# of syncai_robot_state. An image built before that stanza has no underlay, and
# a colcon build that reaches this package fails on the missing crates.
repositories:
  src/syncai_driver_manager:
    type: git
    url: https://github.com/chungweeeei/SyncAI-Robot-Driver-Manager.git
    version: dev
